DBWn: Database Writer
Writes modified data from memory (Buffer Cache) to datafiles.

LGWR: Log Writer
Writes redo information "redo logs buffer" to "Redo log files"

CKPT: Checkpoint process
Updates control files by creating points. 

# Analogy: 
Upto this point, everything has been written safely.

SMON: System Monitor
Handles instance recovery. 

PMON: Process Monitor
Cleans up failed user sessions.

ARCn: Archiver Process
Copies filled Redo logs to "Archive Logs"

RECO: Recoverer process
It is used in distributed databases to automatically resolve failed distributed transactions.

# why RECO:
===========
Imagine a transaction involves two databases. Then oracle uses a 2-Phase-Commit (2PC) Protocol to ensure both databases either "commit together" or "Roll back together".
Particularly used after failure.
